{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Your Thummim and your Urim.</b> The Thummim and also the Urim You gave to Aaron, who was the man and head of the devout tribe, which is the tribe of Levi. By this it is explained that he would speak by the holy spirit and the Shekhinah dwelt upon him, as the Sages of blessed memory said (Yoma 73b): any priest who speaks by the holy spirit and the Shekhinah dwells upon him — inquiries are made of him by the Urim and Thummim." "<b>Whom You tried at Massah.</b> In every trial by which Israel tested the blessed El — as it says: וַיְנַסוּ אוֹתִי זֶה עֶשֶׂר פְּעָמִים (Numbers 14:22) — the tribe of Levi did not test Him, and therefore the decree of the spies was not decreed upon them." "<b>You strove with him at the waters of Meribah.</b> You cut off his two heads, namely Moses and Aaron, on account of the waters of Meribah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:33.273161570Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}